===BODY===
          <h2>Breaking down on a French motorway</h2>
          <p>On French autoroutes, you can't simply call any recovery company. Breakdowns are handled by the official operator approved for that stretch of motorway, at a regulated price. Use the orange emergency phones every 2 km or call 112, and the approved operator will take your car to a safe place off the motorway, usually their own garage. From there, we can take over and bring the car home.</p>

          <h2>What to have with you</h2>
          <p>In France you must carry a reflective vest for every passenger (within reach, not in the boot) and a warning triangle. In cities with low emission zones (ZFE), such as Paris, Lyon, Marseille and others, a Crit&rsquo;Air sticker is required, including for UK cars. If your car breaks down, these zones don't stop it being collected, but they're worth knowing about if you're driving on afterwards.</p>

          <h2>Getting it home</h2>
          <p>Once the car is at a garage or pound, tell us the address, the make and model, whether it rolls and steers, and where it should go in the UK. We give you a fixed price for the whole trip, collect it on a transporter and bring it across via Calais or Dunkirk. From the north of France that can be very quick. From the south it's a longer journey, and we'll tell you the expected timing when we quote.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Tip:</strong> before you leave the car, take photos of it, note the garage name, address and phone number, and make sure the garage knows we'll be collecting it. It saves a lot of time.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Popular collection points</h2>
          <p>We collect from anywhere in France. We have dedicated pages for <a href="{{R}}repatriation/calais.html">Calais</a>, <a href="{{R}}repatriation/paris.html">Paris</a>, <a href="{{R}}repatriation/lille.html">Lille</a>, <a href="{{R}}repatriation/lyon.html">Lyon</a>, <a href="{{R}}repatriation/bordeaux.html">Bordeaux</a>, <a href="{{R}}repatriation/marseille.html">Marseille</a> and <a href="{{R}}repatriation/nice.html">Nice</a>.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: My car was towed off the autoroute by a French operator. Can you collect it from their garage?
A: Yes. That's the usual situation. Send us the garage's name and address, and make sure any fees there are paid and the garage knows we're coming.
Q: Do you speak French with the garage?
A: Yes. We can deal with the French garage directly in French, so you don't have to.
Q: Can my insurer pay for the repatriation?
A: Many European breakdown policies include it. Check your policy first. If you need to arrange it yourself, we'll give you a written quote you can send to your insurer.
